Prerequisites
-------------

The following packages are needed

  - A C++ compiler supporting C++26 (tested with GCC 16)
  - Boost (only the header-only Boost.Tokenizer is used)
  - zlib (optional; to handle Office Open XML documents)
  - The libYGP library. Also available as a Sourceforge project. Get it from
    libymp.sourceforge.net (how inconsistently).


How to build Extract (UNIX-style)
---------------------------------

Additional prerequisite software:

  - Meson (>= 1.5) and Ninja
  - mgeni.pl (from the YGP library)
  - GNU gettext (for national language support)

Inside the directory containing the source code type

  meson setup build [meson-options]
  meson compile -C build
  meson install -C build


Common options for meson
------------------------

Options are passed to "meson setup" (or later to "meson configure build")
as -D<option>=<value>; "meson configure build" lists them all.

  --prefix=<path>               # default: /usr/local
  -Dnls=disabled                # Disable national language support
  -Dplugins=true                # Enable plug-ins (libraries, which extract
                                  information from file-types)
  -Dthreads=true                # Enable thread support - Note that this
                                  can actually even slow down the search.
                                  Use only on multi-processor systems
  -Dchecks=<level>              # Adds asserts and Checks
  -Ddebug-level=<level>         # Sets tracelevel & generation of debuginfo
  -D<filetype>=false            # To disable supporting certain files (html,
                                  jpeg, png, gif, mp3, ogg, pdf, oo, abiword,
                                  rtf, msoffice)

Common commands
---------------

  meson test -C build           # Runs the tests
  meson install -C build        # Installs the whole thing
  ninja -C build clean          # Deletes the files created during the build
  ninja -C build uninstall      # Uninstalls (after you found out what crap
                                  this package actually contains)
  ninja -C build check_code     # Checks the sources with cppcheck
  ninja -C build IExtract-update-po  # Updates the translations in po/


How to build Extract (Windows)
------------------------------

At the moment there exists only a makefile for Visual C++ (6.0). To build
enter the directory where you extracted the sources and execute the included
batch file by typing:

   make

The Makefile tries to link with the static version of the libYGP library. To
make this work, the environment variables LIB and INCLUDE must be set to the
approbiate paths. E.g.:

  set LIB=%LIB%;E:\LIB
  set INCLUDE=%INCLUDE%;E:\Include

Make does *not* set the environment for the compiler, so you might need to run
VCVars32.bat before compiling!


* Common options/targets for make:

  - clean                          # Deletes the files created during the make
